==================================================
1. PRODUCT PURPOSE
==================================================

The platform exists to support the daily work of micro and small enterprises while giving Beacon advisors and administrators a reliable, structured picture of each enterprise's progress toward:

- formalization;
- legal/compliance readiness;
- financial record quality;
- financial readiness;
- financing referral readiness.

The platform must connect the full enterprise journey in ONE enterprise record:

SME onboarding
-> profile
-> bookkeeping
-> documents
-> compliance
-> advisory support
-> readiness assessment
-> MFI matching
-> consent
-> referral
-> financing outcome

The product should replace fragmented spreadsheets and disconnected records with one controlled platform.

Target deployment:
- up to approximately 200 SMEs;
- Damascus;
- Rural Damascus;
- Daraa.

Primary operating realities:
- many transactions may be cash-based;
- users may have limited financial literacy;
- users may have limited digital literacy;
- connectivity may be unreliable;
- Arabic is the primary experience.

==================================================
2. REQUIRED USER ROLES
==================================================

The system must support at minimum these roles:

1. SME_USER
2. BEACON_ADVISOR
3. BEACON_ADMIN
4. MFI_USER
5. TECHNICAL_ADMIN

Permissions must be enforced server-side.

Role visibility in the UI is not authorization.

==================================================
3. ROLE ACCESS REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

### SME_USER

May access only their authorized enterprise data, including as applicable:

- enterprise profile;
- financial records;
- transactions;
- documents;
- compliance requirements;
- readiness actions;
- readiness results;
- AI assistant;
- AI suggestions related to their records;
- referral consents;
- referral status where appropriate.

An SME user must never access another SME's data.

### BEACON_ADVISOR

May access only assigned/permitted enterprises.

Advisor functions include:

- review SME progress;
- review enterprise profile;
- identify incomplete information;
- review financial-record completeness;
- review compliance status;
- review readiness status;
- record technical-assistance/advisory activity;
- create follow-up actions;
- assign responsible persons where allowed;
- set target dates where allowed;
- review referrals and preparation status.

### BEACON_ADMIN

May manage authorized programme functions including:

- users;
- programme records;
- compliance requirements;
- requirement versions;
- readiness/scoring rules;
- MFI eligibility configuration;
- approved knowledge content;
- dashboards;
- programme monitoring configuration;
- other approved administrative settings.

### MFI_USER

May access ONLY referral packages explicitly shared with their own institution.

MFI users must NOT have access to:

- the full SME directory;
- unrelated SMEs;
- referrals for another institution;
- unrelated documents;
- general Beacon programme records.

### TECHNICAL_ADMIN

May manage the technical environment through restricted and documented privileges.

Technical-administrator status must NOT automatically mean unrestricted access to programme/business data.

