9. BOOKKEEPING & FINANCIAL MANAGEMENT
==================================================

The platform must support everyday financial records for each SME.

Minimum supported transaction/business record types:

- income;
- sales;
- purchases;
- expenses;
- receivables;
- payables;
- cash transactions.

Each applicable entry must support at minimum:

- transaction date;
- amount;
- currency;
- category;
- payment status;
- relevant supporting information;
- attachment of receipt/invoice where applicable.

Users must be able to:

- create records;
- view records;
- search records;
- filter records;
- review payment status;
- attach supporting documents;
- correct records through an auditable method.

==================================================
10. FINANCIAL RECORD AUTHORITY
==================================================

Stored transactions and deterministic application rules are the authoritative financial source.

AI is NOT authoritative.

AI must never independently:

- post a transaction;
- change a balance;
- overwrite an authoritative financial value;
- silently modify a financial record.

The user must review AI/OCR suggestions before they become authoritative financial records.

==================================================
11. FINANCIAL POSTING & CORRECTIONS
==================================================

Posted records must not be silently overwritten.

Corrections must preserve audit history.

The application must support an auditable correction approach.

Exact correction workflow must follow the reporting/accounting basis agreed with Beacon.

TODO: BUSINESS DECISION REQUIRED
Confirm the final correction method, for example:
- editable draft before posting + reversal/correction after posting;
- versioned correction records;
- another approved accounting correction procedure.

==================================================
12. DOUBLE-COUNTING CONTROLS
==================================================

The system must prevent financial double counting.

At minimum:

- recording a credit sale and later receiving payment must NOT record revenue twice;
- recording a credit purchase and later paying the supplier must NOT record the expense twice.

These scenarios are mandatory test cases.

==================================================
13. MULTI-CURRENCY BEHAVIOR
==================================================

Where multiple currencies are used, the platform must preserve:

- original amount;
- original currency;
- approved conversion rate where conversion is used.

Historical records must not be silently recalculated using a new exchange rate.

TODO: BUSINESS DECISION REQUIRED
