21. COMPLIANCE VERSIONING
==================================================

Compliance requirements must be versioned.

Every published change must record:

- what changed;
- who changed it;
- when it changed;
- effective version/date as applicable.

Historical assessments must retain the version of the requirement used at the time of assessment.

Example required behavior:

If a document requirement changes after an SME was assessed:

- the old assessment remains viewable under the old rule;
- a new assessment may evaluate the SME against the new rule.

Never rewrite history when a requirement changes.

