69. FUNCTIONAL COMPLETION RULE
==================================================

A module is not functionally complete just because a page exists.

It is complete only when:

- the required business workflow works end-to-end;
- role restrictions work;
- record-level restrictions work;
- server-side validation works;
- required history/versioning works;
- mobile experience works;
- Arabic RTL works;
- loading/error/empty states exist;
- relevant audit events exist;
- required exports/reports work;
- required tests pass;
- unsupported business decisions are explicitly marked rather than invented.

